# Anti-Over-Engineering

Only change what was asked. Prefer the simplest solution that matches existing Page Object Model and locator rules.

## Do not

- Touch unrelated files or rewrite a file for a small edit
- Add helpers, wrappers, or new dependencies without a concrete need
- Introduce extra page-object layers, base classes, or fixture indirection “for later”
- Add error handling for cases that cannot happen in the current flow

## Before finishing

- Diff matches the request
- No new abstraction exists unless the user asked for it or duplication is already real
- When the design is ambiguous, ask instead of inventing architecture
